bashy half of Sprint 531 D3 (Story #59, Story-ID 09ca87a77ca4): a @guard cap
that leaves out net discharges net the way @contain(net: "deny") does.

Apply in the bashy repository (from its root):  git apply PATH/TO/this.patch
Base: bashy 93d5b509ad3c (the ycode go.mod pin). Verified on a copy of that
module: go test -short ./pkg/harnessrunner -run
'TestDecoratedEnvelopeBoundsInterpreters|TestFunctions' passes.

Why: genie's deny remedy now teaches @effects("read,write,exec") +
@guard("read,write,exec") instead of @contain(net: "deny") (no sandbox, no
podman, same on every OS). The harnessrunner compiler still added a possible
net effect (source "uncontained") to any declared envelope without @contain,
so policy asked instead of allowing. With this patch a net-free guard
suppresses that fact. ycode carries the same rule at its executor boundary
(internal/harness/bashy/guard.go) until the bashy pin includes this; it is a
no-op afterwards and can be removed then.

Known limit (recorded for the operator): the
guard is an in-interpreter, atlas-level cap. It denies commands the Command
Atlas classifies with net (fetch, sntp: 126 "denied by the effect cap"). It
does not cross an execve, and under @effects a command the atlas does not
know takes the declared classification: scp and rsync to 127.0.0.1 ran inside
@effects("read,write,exec") + @guard("read,write,exec"), and a child shell
(`sh t.sh` re-entering bashy; observed with bashy c768073) ran curl inside
the guard: the cap is not inherited. This is weaker than
@contain's OS-enforced net deny.
diff -ru a/pkg/harnessrunner/refine_files_test.go b/pkg/harnessrunner/refine_files_test.go
--- a/pkg/harnessrunner/refine_files_test.go	2026-10-29 14:13:34.833955059 -0700
+++ b/pkg/harnessrunner/refine_files_test.go	2026-10-29 14:13:44.434653149 -0700
@@ -175,6 +175,25 @@
 	if _, net := effectKinds(open)[atlas.EffNet]; !net {
 		t.Fatalf("an uncontained declaration without net must keep a possible net effect: %+v", open.Effects)
 	}
+	// S531 D3: a guard that leaves out net discharges it like contain does —
+	// the in-interpreter cap denies net commands, with no sandbox.
+	guarded := compileIn(t, dir, `@effects("read,write,exec")
+@guard("read,write,exec")
+function tests() { sh test_slug.sh; }
+tests`)
+	if !guarded.Complete {
+		t.Fatalf("declared, guarded envelope incomplete: %+v", guarded.Unsupported)
+	}
+	if _, net := effectKinds(guarded)[atlas.EffNet]; net {
+		t.Fatalf("a net-free guard must discharge net: %+v", guarded.Effects)
+	}
+	netGuard := compileIn(t, dir, `@effects("read,write,exec")
+@guard("read,write,exec,net")
+function tests() { sh test_slug.sh; }
+tests`)
+	if _, net := effectKinds(netGuard)[atlas.EffNet]; !net {
+		t.Fatalf("a guard admitting net must keep the possible net effect: %+v", netGuard.Effects)
+	}
 	exceeds := compileIn(t, dir, `@guard("read")
 @effects("read,write")
 function tests() { python3 -m pytest; }
